From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:44:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 045/161] hjviewer: a splash screen in the app's colours, with
 the organisation line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The splash was Flutter's template: white on Android up to 11, black in the dark theme; the
system default on Android 12+; on iOS a white screen with a 1x1 transparent image, white in the
dark theme too. Now Android 6 and later and iOS show the app icon in the middle of the Flutter UI's own
background colour (#FFFFFF light, #18191E dark: MyTheme's scaffold colours), so the first frame
changes nothing, and the line 연세대학교 프로젝트TF small and grey near the bottom (#6B7684
light, #848B97 dark). Light or dark follows the system setting. No animation, no new dependency.

- Android 12+ (values-v31, values-night-v31): the system splash. windowSplashScreenBackground is
  the background colour; windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon is the launcher icon's foreground on a
  240dp canvas, shown in the 160dp circle of windowSplashScreenIconBackgroundColor
  (ic_launcher_background), as the adaptive launcher icon; windowSplashScreenBrandingImage is the
  line. values-night outranks values-v31, so the dark theme needs its own copy.
- Android 6-11 (drawable-v23/launch_background.xml): a layer-list of the same parts, the line 24dp
  above the bottom of the window background, which ends at the navigation bar. Layer-list items
  have no size or gravity before API 23, so API 22 keeps drawable-v21: the background colour.
- values/hjv_splash.xml and values-night/hjv_splash.xml hold the colours.
- The activity names its NormalTheme (io.flutter.embedding.android.NormalTheme, as in Flutter's
  template), whose window background is now the same colour. Without it the launch theme, now with
  the icon and the line, stays behind the Flutter UI, where rotation, the keyboard or a resize can
  show it. The dark window background behind the UI was black; it is #18191E now.
- iOS (LaunchScreen.storyboard): the named colours LaunchBackground and LaunchText with any and
  dark appearances, the LaunchImage tile at 120pt (twice the home screen icon) in the centre, and
  a label with the line in the 13pt system font, 24pt above the bottom of the safe area. The line is
  a proper name and needs no translation.

The drawings come from the hjviewer repository's client/overlay (scripts/make-icons.sh), which
this commit needs: drawable/hjv_splash_icon.xml and drawable/hjv_splash_branding.xml (the line as
glyph outlines of Noto Sans CJK KR; no font file ships) and the iOS LaunchImage PNGs. Windows is
unchanged: its window appears only once Flutter runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
